[br0w+@andrew.cmu.edu (Bruno W. Repetto) writes:]
[] Some minor quirks I found:
[]  - One of the devils is named 'Demogorgon'. Shouldn't it be 'Demigorgon'?
[]  - Zombies should be the ones to turn undead, not trolls.

there is literature that trolls re-animate.  however, i like the
suggestion, perhaps zombies should similarly re-animate from
appropriate corpses (but not as proficiently as trolls).

[]  - Vlad the Impaler should be improved. By the time I get to him, he is
[]    a wimp by comparison.

these things evolve.  we can only hope that in a future version of
nethack that Vlad will be bad ...

[]  - Xorns and Umber Ulks are not currently described in the 'DATA' file.

shouldn't the data file really provide enough info so that the complete
illiterates among us (me included!) can discern what it is we are dealing
with in the dungeon.  i don't like the fact that you have to have a D&D
background to make heads or tails of certain things.  popular literature
is okay (i.e. the delphic oracle) but specialized literature (i.e.
D&D monster manual) ain't!

[] Questions:
[]  - Has the BIG LEVEL been implemented as an option?  I've never
[]    encountered it in my PC NH 3.09 [...]

the bigroom, unfortunately, has its odds of appearing in a given dungeon
set way low.  it should be a feature of every dungeon, IMO.  umm, i do
believe it's in IBM-PC nethack.

[]  - Is there a way to gain an intrinsic that protects one of being
[]     aralyzed by gelatinous cubes and the like once one is powerful enough?

no,  you cannot simply hack and slash every monster you meet!  yeah,
there's the related issue of "i didn't mean to hit the cube ..." but
you have to be on your best behavior when traversing the dungeons of
doom.  let the hacker beware ...

[]  - Should one get the intrinsic of walking through walls after eating or
[]    (maybe) sacrificing xorns?

hmm, probably not (makes things too easy) ...

[]  - Should blessed scrolls of genocide wipe out entire classes of monsters?
[]    (I.e., if one responds with a 'T', trolls, ice trolls, rock trolls,
[]    water trolls, olog hais would be history)

i didn't get the question.  blessed scrolls of genocide currently wipe
out all monsters of a given class (with exceptions).  that's okay (and
historic, somewhat) as long as the classes remain coherent.  perhaps if
it were blessed and _friendly_ it might ask before killing each member
of a class.

[] Stuff left behind by some monsters, once dead:
[]  - Elf corpses should leave elvish stuff.

should change in future versions ...

[]  - Hobbits and wraiths should (sometimes) leave rings.

hobbits sometimes leave behind a weapon which can be named Sting.
note that naming any arbitrary weapon does not make it a special
weapon (artifact).  it has to be a _class_ weapon!

[]  - Crocodiles should (sometimes) leave: a bag of holding, or leather
[]    armor or leather boots.

curiously, if one polymorphs a croc corpse one can get walking shoes.
the bigger the croc, the better, so to speak (no really!) ...

[]  - Ghosts should leave behind (sometimes) a cloak of invisibility, perhaps
[]    cursed?

??? ohh, i get it.  they're wearing sheets ... not really ... ;)

[]  - Credit cards and gems should also be found in vaults (sometimes.)

hmmm, interesting ...

